---
description: Svelte 5 UI conventions for Control and Delivery
globs: "**/*.svelte,**/*.svelte.ts,**/*.svelte.js"
alwaysApply: false
---
Svelte 5 runes only: `$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`, `$props()`, `$bindable()`.
No legacy stores in new code, no `on:click`, no `export let`, no `<slot>`.
Callback props, `{#snippet}` / `{@render}`. Keyed each on ids or slugs.
`$effect` only for attach, analytics, or browser APIs.
Control UI is authenticated and operational and uses `docs/28` identity tokens. Delivery UI uses the client brand tokens.
Do not import Maximum Global Exposure cream or cinema marketing tokens into Vector.
Do not import Control Vector identity tokens into Delivery.
Public delivery pages SSR. Do not fetch internal APIs from public components.
Sanitize untrusted HTML before `{@html}`. Never put secrets in `PUBLIC_` env.
Validate new `.svelte` with Svelte MCP `svelte-autofixer`.
Every list needs skeleton, empty, and error states. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Never fake metrics.
Public marketing, funnel, and conversion UI must also follow `docs/27` and `.cursor/rules/frontend-funnel-quality.mdc`.
Control product UI must also follow `docs/28` and `.cursor/rules/vector-visual-language.mdc`.
First client website reveal UI is Control (`docs/28`) wrapping a Delivery preview (`docs/27`, `docs/plans/FIRST_REVEAL_TRACK.md`).
